Read this data processing agreement:
{{brief}}

Check it against GDPR Article 28(3). For each point say PRESENT, WEAK or MISSING, with the clause number: processing only on documented instructions; confidentiality of staff; security measures (Article 32); rules for sub-processors; help with requests from data subjects; help with security, breach notices and impact assessments; deletion or return at the end; audits and information. Then list any transfer outside the EEA and the safeguard it names.

Read the same agreement:
{{brief}}

List the business risks: limits of liability, who pays for audits, how many hours the processor has to report a breach, and anything that lets the processor change the terms alone.

Write a one-page memo for the person who signs. The verdict first: sign, sign after changes, or do not sign. Then the changes to ask for, the most important first, each with a suggested wording.

